# {{.App}}

A SvelteKit application served by Go. VitePlus and `sv` created the frontend;
skgo added the Go server and bindings. Node is a build-time and development
dependency, not a production runtime dependency.

## Prerequisites

- Go {{.GoVersion}} or newer
- Node 22.17 or newer
- pnpm and `just`

The generator installed frontend dependencies, Chromium for the generated
Vitest component test, and an initial frontend build. None of those are
committed. In a fresh clone `just dev` installs the dependencies and makes that
build once, when it finds them missing; the component test additionally needs
`pnpm --dir web exec playwright install chromium`.

## Development

```sh
just dev
```

Open {{.Origin}}. Edit a Svelte component under `web/src/` and the normal
VitePlus development workflow updates the page.

Storybook and Vitest are ready to run:

```sh
just storybook
just test
```

## Production

```sh
just build
./bin/{{.App}}
```

The resulting binary embeds the frontend build and serves it without Node.
{{if .Examples}}
## Go examples

The home page calls the query and command in
`web/src/routes/example.remote.go`. `skgo generate` creates the matching
TypeScript module with throwing server stubs, so the displayed status and the
write interaction can only be answered by Go.
{{end}}
